  Let $M$ be a $3$-connected matroid and let $N$ be a $3$-connected minor of $M$.
  We say that a triangle or triad~$T$ of $M$ is \emph{\unfortunate} if, for all distinct $a,b \in T$, none of $M\/a\/b$, $M\/a\ba b$, $M\ba a\/b$, and $M\ba a\ba b$ have an $N$-minor.

  \begin{lemma}[{\cite[Lemma~3.1]{paper1}}]
    \label{freegrounded}
    Let $M$ be a $3$-connected matroid with a $3$-connected minor $N$ where 
    $|E(N)| \ge 4$.
    If $T$ is an \unfortunate\ triangle of $M$ with $x \in T$, 
    then $x$ is not $N$-contractible.
