A bi-action between \'etale groupoids $G$ and $H$ is a span of locales $G_0\leftarrow X\rightarrow H_0$ together with a left $G$-action and a right $H$-action on $X$ satisfying natural conditions. It can be thought of as a binary relation between the generalized spaces (in the topos sense) of orbits of the groupoids. The corresponding notion of functional relation is that of a Hilsum--Skandalis map~ \cites{Moer90,Moer87,Bunge,MRW87,La01,Mr99,HS87}. Concretely, thi

