\begin{abstract}
In this paper we show that every set $A \subset \mathbb{N}$ with positive density
contains $B+C$ for some pair $B,C$ of infinite subsets of $\mathbb{N}$, settling a conjecture of Erd\H{o}s{}.
The proof features two different decompositions of an arbitrary bounded sequence into a structured component and a pseudo-random component.
Our methods are quite general, allowing us to prove a version of this conjecture for countable amenable groups.
\end{abstract}


