Embodied AI (EAI) refers to artificial intelligence (AI) systems and agents that are grounded in the physical world and learn through perception and action~\cite{paolo_call_2024, liu_aligning_2024}. EAI systems can operate across diverse environments. For example, existing EAI applications can deliver packages~\cite{li_drone-aided_2023}, patrol public spaces as security guards~\cite{qiongfang_chinese_2024}, or care for humans in intimate settings such as elder-care homes~\cite{takenaka_ai_2025, kim_ai_2025}. EAI capabilities and domains are likely to expand significantly in the coming years~\cite{garlick2024airobots, suleyman_coming_2023}. 

